hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27747","Haddathana Hafs ibn Ghiyath who said: Haddathana al-Amash from Adi ibn Thabit al-Ansari from Sulayman ibn Surad: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard two men while they were disputing, and one of them had become angry and his anger had intensified, and he was speaking; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know a word which, if he said it, the devil would go from him; he said: So a man came to him and said: Say: I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed devil; he said: Do you see harm in me; he said: He did not add to that."
"27748","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Sufyan who said: Haddathani Abu Ishaq who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Surad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Confederates: Now we attack them and they do not attack us."
"27749","Haddathana Yunus ibn Muhammad who said: Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Maysara Abu Layla from Abu Ukkasha al-Hamdani who said: Rifaa al-Bajali said: I entered upon al-Mukhtar ibn Abi Ubayd in his palace and heard him say: Jibril has only just risen from with me; he said: So I intended to strike his neck, then I remembered a hadith told to us by Sulayman ibn Surad from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: If a man entrusts you with his blood, do not kill him; he said: And he had entrusted me with his blood, so I disliked his blood."
